80
00:02:53,030 --> 00:02:55,730
that a single sentence can solve this problem.

81
00:02:55,730 --> 00:02:56,510
That's all just a scam.

82
00:02:56,510 --> 00:02:58,010
And that's why so many bosses end up getting scammed.

83
00:02:58,010 --> 00:02:59,090
And that's where their delusions get really big.

84
00:02:59,090 --> 00:03:02,540
He probably thinks, 'Isn't this super simple for a product manager to do?'

85
00:03:02,540 --> 00:03:04,380
Didn't it just spit out this page with a single command?

86
00:03:04,380 --> 00:03:05,780
And then they take my project and show it to others, telling them,

87
00:03:05,780 --> 00:03:07,900
Look, they just spit this out with a single prompt.

88
00:03:07,900 --> 00:03:09,540
way better than your fancy UI design work,

89
00:03:09,540 --> 00:03:13,210
and looks way better than that... uh... Adobe whatever thing you handmade.

90
00:03:13,210 --> 00:03:13,730
Right?

91
00:03:13,730 --> 00:03:14,690
So, how do you explain this?

92
00:03:14,690 --> 00:03:16,330
So, aren't they all just scams?

93
00:03:16,330 --> 00:03:23,160
So, this is what we're talking about. Something that looks like it works on the surface and something that actually works are two completely different things.

94
00:03:23,160 --> 00:03:24,140
They're worlds apart.

95
00:03:24,140 --> 00:03:28,740
Right, so this is the point I've been making: don't just fall for those claims. It's not that simple.

96
00:03:28,740 --> 00:03:31,250
So, using AI is really not that simple. Okay?

97
00:03:31,250 --> 00:03:32,810
So, here's the field list.

98
00:03:32,810 --> 00:03:34,210
So, once you've got that field list,

99
00:03:34,210 --> 00:03:36,110
But actually, we also need a business process workflow.

100
00:03:36,110 --> 00:03:37,810
But I actually missed something here.

101
00:03:37,810 --> 00:03:39,130
So, what does this business process derivation entail?

102
00:03:39,130 --> 00:03:42,610
Basically, I need to have a clear idea of the relationship between this purchase order and all the documents that fall under it.

103
00:03:42,610 --> 00:03:44,959
Its object modeling,

104
00:03:44,959 --> 00:03:46,279
This kind of entity-relationship modeling.

105
00:03:46,279 --> 00:03:47,519
What's the one-to-many relationship ratio?

106
00:03:47,519 --> 00:03:49,579
And then, what are the key states for each of them?

107
00:03:49,579 --> 00:03:52,450
And then, what's the sequence of interactions between them? You know, what happens first, and what happens next.

108
00:03:52,450 --> 00:03:53,430
and its corresponding logical deductions.

109
00:03:53,430 --> 00:03:55,220
I need to have a general flow like this.

110
00:03:55,220 --> 00:03:56,660
so the AI can understand the process.

111
00:03:56,660 --> 00:03:56,900
Right?

112
00:03:56,900 --> 00:03:57,580
But that's not included here.

113
00:03:57,580 --> 00:03:59,340
So, since it's missing that information here...

