00:04:36,380 --> 00:04:39,560
So don't be so quick to ask for help.

138
00:04:39,560 --> 00:04:40,800
So you don't need to ask anyone else for help with this.

139
00:04:40,800 --> 00:04:41,820
You can handle it yourself.

140
00:04:41,820 --> 00:04:43,620
So, this is a business PRD.

141
00:04:43,620 --> 00:04:45,960
So, for a business PRD, here are the standard playbooks we usually follow.

142
00:04:45,960 --> 00:04:46,980
You know, the background and all that.

143
00:04:46,980 --> 00:04:48,060
functional scope,

144
00:04:48,060 --> 00:04:49,860
and then any lists of items,

145
00:04:49,860 --> 00:04:50,820
to-do lists,

146
00:04:50,820 --> 00:04:52,280
And then, you know, flowcharts.

147
00:04:52,280 --> 00:04:53,420
Entity-relationship descriptions,

148
00:04:53,420 --> 00:04:54,420
business scenarios,

149
00:04:54,420 --> 00:04:55,980
state machine models,

150
00:04:55,980 --> 00:04:57,700
And a state transition table.

151
00:04:57,700 --> 00:04:59,320
the action capability matrix...

152
00:04:59,320 --> 00:05:01,540
Basically, it's about which operations can be performed in which states.

153
00:05:01,540 --> 00:05:03,860
And then you have its core business rules.

154
00:05:03,860 --> 00:05:05,340
and so on and so forth for all these rules.

155
00:05:05,340 --> 00:05:07,950
And also, some of the underlying logic for how things are processed.

156
00:05:07,950 --> 00:05:09,590
And we've also got the permission design to think about.

157
00:05:09,590 --> 00:05:11,910
And then there are the non-functional requirements, right?

158
00:05:11,910 --> 00:05:13,580
You know, things like edge case handling.

159
00:05:13,580 --> 00:05:14,180
handling for all those,

160
00:05:14,180 --> 00:05:14,700
and how those are handled.

161
00:05:14,700 --> 00:05:17,380
and also things like the acceptance criteria, and so on.

162
00:05:17,380 --> 00:05:20,810
So, a lot of people might say, 'Back in the day, when I used to design...'

